<title>GREECE: GREEK BROKERS' MARKET SHARES IN DECEMBER- SMEHA.</title>
<headline>GREEK BROKERS' MARKET SHARES IN DECEMBER- SMEHA.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trading volume at the Athens bourse</p>
<p>in December rose to 577.16 billion drachmas from 366.03 billion</p>
<p>in November, the Athens stock exchange members association</p>
<p>(SMEHA) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>National Bank subsidiary National Securities led</p>
<p>in market share with 43.09 percent of the bourse's trading</p>
<p>volume helped by active block trading.</p>
<p>The exchange's 63 other members shared the remaining 56.9</p>
<p>percent.</p>
<p>It was followed by Alpha Credit Bank subsidiary</p>
<p>Alpha Brokerage with 12.2 percent.</p>
<p>Ranking third was Sigma Securities with 6.2 percent followed</p>
<p>by Kappa Securities in fourth place with 5.17 percent.</p>
<p>Cumulative January-to-December 1996 trading volume reached</p>
<p>3.979 trillion drachmas. The last month of the year turned out</p>
<p>to be the best month with turnover hitting 577 billion while May</p>
<p>was the worst with 209 billion drachmas.</p>
<p>SMEHA released the following data and market share rankings</p>
<p>for December. The top 15 brokers shared 86.9 percent of the</p>
<p>bourse's trading volume leaving 13.1 percent for the other 49</p>
<p>brokers.</p>
<p>    BROKER    NOV RANK   VOLUME DECEMBER    MARKET SHARE</p>
<p>				 (in drs billion)</p>
<p> 1. National    (1)	   248.70		 43.09%</p>
<p> 2. Alpha	 (5)	    70.42		 12.20%</p>
<p> 3. Sigma	 (2)	    35.77		  6.20%</p>
<p> 4. Kappa	 (18)	   29.81		  5.17%</p>
<p> 5. Commercial  (27)	   24.49		  4.24%</p>
<p> 6. Telesis     (6)	    15.90		  2.76%</p>
<p> 7. Devletoglou (5)	    15.73		  2.73%</p>
<p> 8. Hermes	(24)	   12.78		  2.21%</p>
<p> 9. Aspis	 (8)	     8.31		  1.44%</p>
<p>10. Eurosec     (25)	    8.26		  1.43%</p>
<p>11. ABN AMRO    (19)	    7.26		  1.26%</p>
<p>12. Avax	  (11)	    6.62		  1.15%</p>
<p>13. Omega	 (17)	    6.13		  1.06%</p>
<p>14. Midland     (7)	     6.10		  1.06%</p>
<p>15. P &amp; K	 (20)	    5.55		  0.96%</p>
<p>    Total volume		577.16</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
